  "worked_solution": "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-4$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=4$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-4$, $x=0$, and $x=4.$",
